# ============================================================================
# Phase 7 Scenario 4 — Syringe Services Program (SSP) saturation
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intent: every PWID has SSP access, reducing injection-related HIV transmission.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-17. The path is confirmed and SSP is fully wired — the
# previous version's "if SSP is NOT yet a wired feature, that's an engine gap"
# no longer applies. features.syringe_services is True in the calibration base
# and tests/…::test_syringe_services passes, which closed the 2026-07-30 finding
# that syringe services did not reduce HIV incidence.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PATH, AND WHAT EACH FIELD MEANS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# titan/params/syringe_services.yml defines a `timeline` of named periods. The
# calibration base carries one, `ssp_open`:
#
#     syringe_services:
#       timeline:
#         ssp_open:
#           num_slots_start: 71     # enrolment CAP, an absolute agent count
#           num_slots_stop:  71     # differing start/stop makes a linear ramp
#           risk: 0.16              # unsafe-sharing probability once enrolled
#           start_time: -999        # ENCORE has run continuously since 1994
#           stop_time:  999
#
# Anchors: ENCORE's operating history sets the times; NHBS-PWID 2018 gives 55%
# SSP reach and 26% receptive sharing. The out-of-SSP counterfactual is
# demographics.*.injection.unsafe_prob = 0.38.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO TRAPS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. num_slots IS AN ABSOLUTE COUNT AND DOES NOT SCALE WITH N. At N=500 the model
#    holds ~88 PWID (Inj.ppl 0.176 x 500), so 71 slots is ~81% reach. If Stage A2
#    raises N, a hard-coded slot count silently stops being saturation. Set it far
#    above any N the analysis will use.
#
# 2. BASELINE REACH IS ALREADY HIGH. 81% in the model against NHBS-PWID's 55%
#    observed. Saturation therefore buys only ~19 percentage points of reach, so
#    this arm will look weak, and that is a property of the baseline rather than
#    of the intervention. Check the 71 against the refit's PWID count before
#    running, and say in the paper what baseline reach the contrast starts from.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FILL IN — Jun
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Saturate REACH, not per-act risk: `risk` is the residual sharing probability of
# someone who is enrolled, and it is anchored to NHBS-PWID's 26% receptive
# sharing. Lowering it as well would conflate two different interventions
# (more coverage vs safer behaviour within coverage) and make the arm
# uninterpretable. Change slots only, unless you deliberately want the joint arm.
#
# ============================================================================
# syringe_services:
#   timeline:
#     ssp_open:
#       num_slots_start: 100000    # >> any N; unconditional access
#       num_slots_stop:  100000
#       risk: 0.16                 # UNCHANGED — see above
